From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: clear DRM device pointer on initialization failure

When component or KMS initialization fails, priv->dev retains the DRM
device pointer after its reference is dropped. msm_kms_shutdown later
dereferences that pointer to check registered, allowing a use-after-free
on a subsequent reboot. Clear the pointer on both initialization failure
paths. SM-T531 native bring-up reproduced a shutdown loss of console after
a KMS ENODEV failure; the dangling pointer is established by code review,
while the physical shutdown cause awaits pstore evidence.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_drv.c
index fa46ab306..e00ee2c0a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_drv.c
@@ -98,6 +98,7 @@ static int msm_drm_uninit(struct device *dev, const struct component_ops *gpu_op
 		component_unbind_all(dev, ddev);
 
 	ddev->dev_private = NULL;
+	priv->dev = NULL;
 	drm_dev_put(ddev);
 
 	return 0;
@@ -186,6 +187,7 @@ static int msm_drm_init(struct device *dev, const struct drm_driver *drv,
 	return ret;
 
 err_put_dev:
+	priv->dev = NULL;
 	drm_dev_put(ddev);
 
 	return ret;
